fact WorkItem(id: "WI-192", description: some(value: "Domain store sorts: refine the generic `Store` with domain-specific operations. Pure use of existing anthill machinery — sort + entity + operation + effects, no new keyword. Surface: a project declares `sort WorkItemStore { requires Store; entity wis(backend: Store, by_id: Map[K = String, V = WorkItem], by_status: Map[K = WorkStatus, V = List[T = WorkItem]], id_counter: Int); operation next_id(s: WorkItemStore) -> String; operation lookup(s: WorkItemStore, id: String) -> Option[T = WorkItem]; operation by_status(s: WorkItemStore, st: WorkStatus) -> List[T = WorkItem]; operation commit(s: WorkItemStore, w: WorkItem) -> Unit effects {Modify[s], Error} }`. The 'indexes' are just named fields on the `wis` entity constructor — Map values populated once at startup, maintained on commit via the Modify[s] effect. The bundle's host (run_anthill_bundle) constructs the initial wis(...) instance from the project's existing facts and passes it to Main.main alongside the other host-supplied resources (the IndexedFileStore is the `backend` field). Bundle command bodies stop using facts_of(kb(), \"WorkItem\") + manual map-building; they take a WorkItemStore and call domain ops directly (`store.next_id()`, `store.lookup(id)`, `store.by_status(Open)`, `store.commit(wi)`). Generalizes: any project declares its own domain stores (UserStore, ProjectStore, ...); composable refinements (FeedbackStore could refine WorkItemStore). Subsumes WI-183's per-command map-building (the maps are now store fields, kept current by commit) and WI-194's commit op (commit is the WorkItemStore's mutation entry point, with the Modify[s] effect handling rollback if a future Error fires). Work: (a) declare WorkItemStore + wis entity + operations in the project's domain.anthill or a new store.anthill; (b) host constructs the initial wis(...) at startup — backend ← IndexedFileStore as today, by_id/by_status/id_counter ← computed from existing facts; (c) Main.main signature gains a WorkItemStore parameter; (d) port bundle command bodies to use the domain ops; (e) the runtime needs no new mechanism — Modify[s] on commit propagates index updates the same way it propagates persist/flush. Acceptance: bundle's main.anthill drops build_row_map / build_dep_map / feedback_set / next_workitem_id / max_id_in / id_suffix_of / parse_wi_suffix / parse_int_or_zero / parse_int_acc / digit_value / pad3 — ~120 lines of glue retire — replaced by domain ops on the store sort; cargo test green; perf parity or better with WI-183 (the maps are still O(1) lookups, just shifted from per-command rebuild to store-field maintenance)."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: nil), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Open)
